  "claims": [
    "IS2-A1: the six gnd-induce sentence changes are each pinned by a test that fails on the IS1 wording",
    "The recorder's checks (no_apply_call, no_hand_written_proposal, actor_from_user, no_forbidden_bash, no_outside_path, done) compute what spec 6.2 and findings F4, F6, F8 say, for any legal stream, not only the recorded ones",
    "spent() counts the example's runs, the evidence attempts and F2, so the USD 10 ceiling is enforced across attempts",
    "render_replay pairs each tool result with its call by id and marks a flattened code fence, without changing any other existing replay",
    "The learn-rules page shows no command outside replay transcripts and recorded user turns, every You type fence is a recorded declared turn (step 6's review prompt marked Not recorded), and every In this run note is true of its transcript",
    "TUTORIAL_CLAIMS' recording column names a string each recording's kept turns actually hold",
    "release_text's replay exclusion and test_ik6_walk's JSON-decoded scan do not hide a real stale claim or a real absolute path in a page or example file"
  ],
